{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 7 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 7 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nProf. Vasechkin wants to represent positive integer n as a sum of addends, where each addends is an integer number containing only 1s. For example, he can represent 121 as 121=111+11+\u20131. Help him to find the least number of digits 1 in such sum.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 7 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static long[] A;\n    private static Map<Long, Long> CACHE;\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        br.close();\n        \n        A = new long[17];\n        A[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i < 17; i++) {\n            A[i] = A[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n        }\n        \n        CACHE = new HashMap<>();\n        System.out.println(compute(n));\n    }\n    \n    private static long compute(long x) {\n        if (x == 0) return 0;\n        if (CACHE.containsKey(x)) return CACHE.get(x);\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < 17; i++) {\n            if (A[i] >= x) {\n                if (A[i] == x) {\n                    long res = i + 1;\n                    CACHE.put(x, res);\n                    return res;\n                }\n                \n                long k = x / A[i - 1];\n                long cost1 = i * k + compute(x - A[i - 1] * k);\n                \n                long diff = A[i] - x;\n                k = diff / A[i - 1];\n                long cost2 = i + 1 + i * k + compute(A[i] - A[i - 1] * k - x);\n                \n                long minCost = Math.min(cost1, cost2);\n                CACHE.put(x, minCost);\n                return minCost;\n            }\n        }\n        throw new IllegalStateException(\"No solution found for \" + x);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static long[] A;\n    private static Map<Long, Long> CACHE;\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine().trim());\n        br.close();\n        \n        A = new long[17];\n        A[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i < 17; i++) {\n            A[i] = A[i-1] * 10 + 1;\n        }\n        \n        CACHE = new HashMap<>();\n        System.out.println(compute(n));\n    }\n    \n    private static long compute(long x) {\n        if (x == 0) return 0;\n        if (x < 0) {\n            x = -x;\n        }\n        if (CACHE.containsKey(x)) return CACHE.get(x);\n        \n        long minCost = Long.MAX_VALUE;\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < 17; i++) {\n            if (A[i] >= x) {\n                if (A[i] == x) {\n                    long res = i + 1;\n                    CACHE.put(x, res);\n                    return res;\n                }\n                \n                // Use positive addends only\n                long k = x / A[i - 1];\n                long cost1 = (i) * k + compute(x - A[i - 1] * k);\n                minCost = Math.min(minCost, cost1);\n                \n                // Use one larger addend and subtract\n                long diff = A[i] - x;\n                if (diff <= x) { // Only consider if it's not too far\n                    long k2 = diff / A[i - 1];\n                    if (k2 <= i) { // Reasonable bound\n                        long cost2 = (i + 1) + (i) * k2 + compute(A[i] - A[i - 1] * k2 - x);\n                        minCost = Math.min(minCost, cost2);\n                    }\n                }\n                \n                CACHE.put(x, minCost);\n                return minCost;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Fallback: use all 1s\n        long res = x;\n        CACHE.put(x, res);\n        return res;\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.095255518332124e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, 0.0, -9.179073458653875e-06, -1.585470999998506e-05, -2.622600959512056e-06, -3.814689989667386e-06, -3.40932747349143e-05, -3.099436753473128e-06, 0.0, -1.7046782886609435e-05, -3.933898824470816e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.861018856492592e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -2.5152843591058627e-05, -1.7165990357170813e-05, -8.821448318485636e-06, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.004280927591025829, -6.6756979322235566e-06, -0.0009126074146479368, -4.0531076592742465e-06, -7.033323527139146e-06, -0.0012334127677604556, -4.470248313737102e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0012309125158935785, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0003383779258001596, -4.6491513785440475e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.145764938177308e-06, -4.410734163684538e-06, 0